                            "note": {
                                "variant": "info",
                                "icon": "mdi-information",
                                "body": "**\u201c10-year return period flood\u201d** does not mean it happens exactly once every 10 years. It means there is a *10% chance* of a flood this size being exceeded in any given year.\n\nReturn period and flood extent:\n- A 10-year flood covers the smallest extent of the scenarios shown here\n- It is the most frequent, but least severe, event modelled\n\nLearn more about [return periods](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Return_period)."
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "value": "50",
