                                "variant": "info",
                                "icon": "mdi-information",
                                "body": "**\u201c50-year return period flood\u201d** does not mean it happens exactly once every 50 years. It means there is a *2% chance* of a flood this size being exceeded in any given year.\n\nReturn period and flood extent:\n- A 50-year flood covers a larger area than a 10-year flood\n- But a smaller area than 100- or 500-year events\n\nLearn more about [return periods](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Return_period)."
