                "note": {
                    "variant": "info",
                    "icon": "mdi-information",
                    "body": "**Depth is what turns water into a hazard**\n\nFrom above, a harmless puddle and a dangerous flood can look exactly the same. To measure real flood risk, we draw the line at **30 cm**:\n\n- **Above 30 cm (light red):** Deep enough to trap people. This counts as exposure.\n- **Below 30 cm (light blue):** Shallow water. This is ignored."
